callee is arbitrary: it may change state, throw any represented exception,
return any value of its result carrier, or diverge.  Receipts record actual
calls, arguments and outcomes.  Their contracts concern order, forwarding,
error identity and state conservation, not a second execution of the body.
A body may diverge only if at least one of its selected callees is not total.
The totality clause is an observation invariant, never a callee-correctness
hypothesis or a restriction on the quantified operation records.
